# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 3b (partner opens 1S). 1NT with a singleton, per Mike.
title: Partner opens 1♠: no perfect answer
id: L02-12
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3
student: S
board: 12
dealer: W
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AQ853  K7     K62    984
  E  K42    J942   J983   KQ
  S  7      AQT65  Q75    JT73
  W  JT96   83     AT4    A652

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1S     = 13+ points, at least four spades
  E Pass
  S 1NT*   = 6-9 points
     key: Our bidding rules have no good response to 1♠ here. The hand isn't really balanced, but it isn't strong enough for 2♥. We'd rather tell a small lie about our distribution than exaggerate our strength.
     not 2H: 2♥ promises 10+ points. Did you count 9?
     not Pass: Did you count 9? With 6 or more, find a response.
     not 2S: Is one spade enough support to raise?
     not *: With 6-9 points and no spade support, which response is closest to the truth?
  W Pass
  N Pass   = A minimum: no game
  E Pass

auction recap:
  With 9 points and a singleton spade, there was no perfect bid. 1NT told
  partner the most important thing, your strength. Partner has a minimum,
  so your side has about 22: no game. You are declarer, because you bid
  no-trump first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W SJ  N SQ  E SK  S S7
  2   E D3  S D5  W DT  N DK
  3   N HK  E H2  S H5  W H3
      note: The plan: take your top hearts and hope the ♥J falls. Dummy's ♥K first, the high card from the short side.
  4   N H7  E H9  S HA  W H8
      note: A heart to your ♥A.
  5   S HQ  W C2  N S3  E H4
      note: The ♥Q. The jack hasn't fallen, so East still has it.
  6   S C3  W C5  N C8  E CQ
      note: You have no way back to your hand for the last hearts, so try the clubs.
  7   E DJ  S DQ  W DA  N D2
  8   W D4  N D6  E D8  S D7
  9   E S2  S C7  W S9  N SA
  10  N C4  E CK  S CJ  W C6
      note: Another club. The defenders take the rest.
  11  E D9  S CT  W S6  N C9
  12  E HJ  S H6  W CA  N S5
  13  E S4  S HT  W ST  N S8
      note: 5 tricks: 1NT down two.

play recap:
  The plan: take your top hearts and hope the ♥J falls.

  1NT down two. East held four hearts to the jack, and with no way back to
  your hand, the long hearts never scored. That was a sound contract, but
  the cards just weren't breaking your way. Your 1NT was a small white lie
  about your shape, but it told partner your strength, and that was what
  mattered.
